EXAM_DATA.papers["1999"] = {"id":"1999","year":1999,"label":"1999 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/1999/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: For each numbered blank in the following passage, there are four choices marked ［A］, ［B］, ［C］ and ［D］. Choose the best one and mark your answer on ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets with a pencil. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Industrial safety does not just happen. Companies   {{1}}   low accident rates plan their safety programs, work hard to organize them, and continue working to keep them   {{2}}   and active. When the work is well done, a   {{3}}   of accident-free operations is established   {{4}}   time lost due to injuries is kept at a minimum."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"Successful safety programs may   {{5}}   greatly in the emphasis placed on certain aspects of the program. Some place great emphasis on mechanical guarding. Others stress safe work practices by   {{6}}   rules or regulations.   {{7}}   others depend on an emotional appeal to the worker. But, there are certain basic ideas that must be used in every program if maximum results are to be obtained."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"There can be no question about the value of a safety program. From a financial standpoint alone, safety   {{8}}   . The fewer the injury   {{9}}   , the better the workman's insurance rate. This may mean the difference between operating at   {{10}}   or at a loss."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"at"},{"key":"B","text":"in"},{"key":"C","text":"on"},{"key":"D","text":"with"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"1.","reason":"Companies + low accident rates 表\"拥有\"关系 线索就在本句 Companies __(1)__ low accident rates plan their safety programs：主句说\"这类公司会规划自己的安全计划\"，反推空格短语在描述\"具有/拥有低事故率\"的那类公司，是定语后置而非地点状语。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"at 常用于 at a rate of...（以……的速率/比率），强调数值本身，不能表达\"公司拥有低事故率\"这种归属关系。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"in 用作 in low accident rates 时偏向\"处于低事故率的状态/领域中\"，硬套到 Companies 后面既不自然，也不能体现\"事故率属于该公司\"这一归属义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"on 与 accident rates 之间没有固定搭配，无法表达 \"公司具有低事故率\" 之意，属于形近介词干扰。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"with 与 Companies 构成 \"Companies with low accident rates\"，即\"具有低事故率的公司\"，with 表伴随特征/具有，正与 Companies __(1)__ low accident rates plan their safety programs 想表达的\"那些拥有低事故率的公司会规划安全计划\"完全吻合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"alive"},{"key":"B","text":"vivid"},{"key":"C","text":"mobile"},{"key":"D","text":"diverse"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"and active 提示\"持续运作\" 本句 continue working to keep them __(2)__ and active 中 continue working 与 active（活跃运作中）共同把\"安全计划处于运作状态\"框死，空格需与 active 同向，即\"保持有生命力、持续运行\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"alive 在英语中常与 active 并列使用，表示\"有生命力的、活跃的\"，可形容计划、组织持续运作的状态，与 keep them __(2)__ and active 想强调的\"让安全计划保持生机与活跃\"完全契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"vivid 多形容色彩、记忆、描写\"鲜明生动\"，不形容计划/制度的活跃运作，与 active 的语义方向偏离。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"mobile 意为\"可移动的、流动的\"，多用于设备、人员等物理移动，与\"让安全计划保持活力\"的抽象语义不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"diverse 意为\"多样的、各异的\"，是\"种类\"维度而非\"活力\"维度，与 active 不构成同向并列，属于偷换概念干扰。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"regulation"},{"key":"B","text":"climate"},{"key":"C","text":"circumstance"},{"key":"D","text":"requirement"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"establish a ___ of operations 提示\"建立……氛围\" 本句 a __(3)__ of accident-free operations is established 表示\"无事故运行的某种东西被建立起来\"，结合后半句 time lost due to injuries is kept at a minimum 可知作者强调的是一种持续、普遍存在的安全状态——也就是\"氛围/环境\"，而不是单条规章或一次性情境。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"regulation 指\"规章、条例\"，是离散的单条文件，无法对应 \"无事故运行\" 这种整体状态；且第二段才提到 rules or regulations，此处尚未到具体规章层面。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"climate 除\"气候\"外，常作\"风气、氛围\"讲，如 a climate of fear。a climate of accident-free operations 即\"无事故运行的整体风气/氛围\"，正与 established（建立起来）以及第一段 plan their safety programs 强调的\"持续状态\"严丝合缝。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"circumstance 意为\"具体情境、情况\"，常以复数出现表客观条件，不能被 establish（建立）；与\"无事故运行的整体状态\"语义错位。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"requirement 是\"要求、必备条件\"，描述的是\"要达到无事故所提出的条件\"，而本句强调的是\"无事故的状态已被建立\"，方向相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"where"},{"key":"B","text":"how"},{"key":"C","text":"what"},{"key":"D","text":"unless"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"4.","reason":"后句是完整句，表\"在该状态下\" 后句 time lost due to injuries is kept at a minimum 是 \"主语 + 谓语 + 状语\" 的完整句子，不缺主宾；且语义上它描述的是在前句\"无事故氛围被建立\"这一状态/场景之中工伤损失被压到最小，正是\"在……的场合里\" 这种抽象\"地点/场景\"关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"where 在书面英语中可引导抽象\"场景/情形\"的状语从句，相当于 in which/in such a situation that，正好把 a __(3)__ of accident-free operations is established 这一\"已建立的氛围\"作为后句发生的背景串起来。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"how 引导方式状语，意为\"以……的方式\"，但前句讲的是\"氛围已建立\"，后句讲\"工伤损失被压到最小\"，两者是\"在该氛围下→产生该结果\"的场景关系，而非\"以氛围这种方式做某事\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"what 作连接词时必须在从句中充当主/宾/表语，而后句 time lost due to injuries is kept at a minimum 已经主谓齐全，没有 what 可以充当的成分，句法上不成立。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"unless 意为\"除非\"，引入否定条件，会变成\"除非工伤损失被压到最小，无事故氛围才被建立\"，与第一段\"主动规划→自然形成低事故\"的因果方向完全相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"alter"},{"key":"B","text":"differ"},{"key":"C","text":"shift"},{"key":"D","text":"distinguish"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"下文列举各家做法 → 反推上句讲\"差异\" 下文用 Some place great emphasis on mechanical guarding. Others stress safe work practices 和 __(7)__ others depend on an emotional appeal 三组 some/others/still others 并列，明显在铺陈\"不同公司的不同做法\"，反推空句必然在说各家计划\"互有差异\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"alter 是\"改变（自身）\"，强调\"由 A 变为 B\"，无法表达\"多家计划之间互不相同\"的横向差异。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"differ 与介词 in 构成固定搭配 differ in sth，正表\"在某方面相互不同\"，与下文 Some/Others/Still others 的并列举例完全呼应。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"shift 意为\"转移、转换（重心、立场）\"，强调时间/方向上的移动，不表达\"不同计划相互之间的差异\"。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"distinguish 意为\"区分、分辨\"，是及物动词，常作 distinguish A from B，本句之后并无被区分的宾语，句法与语义都不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"constituting"},{"key":"B","text":"aggravating"},{"key":"C","text":"observing"},{"key":"D","text":"justifying"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"6.","reason":"stress safe work practices 是目的，手段须\"遵守\" 本句 Others stress safe work practices by __(6)__ rules or regulations. 中主句目的是\"强调安全工作方法\"，与之配套的手段对\"规章\"的合理动作只能是\"遵守/执行\"——制定（constitute）、加重（aggravate）、辩护（justify）都不能达成\"让人去践行安全规范\"这一目的。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"constituting 意为\"构成\"，少见作\"制定规章\"用；即便理解为制定，也只是\"立规\"，未触及\"践行\"，无法直接推出\"强调安全实践\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"aggravating 意为\"加重、恶化\"，带负向色彩，加重规章不能用来强调安全实践，与文段中性—正向的论述基调冲突。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"observing 除\"观察\"外，常表\"遵守（规则/规章/节日）\"，observe rules or regulations 是固定搭配，正可承接 stress safe work practices 这一目的——通过让员工遵守规章来强调安全实践。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"justifying 意为\"为……辩护、证明……合理\"，是事后说理，不是把规则落地为安全实践的手段，与上下文目的不搭。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Some"},{"key":"B","text":"Many"},{"key":"C","text":"Even"},{"key":"D","text":"Still"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"7.","reason":"Some...Others...Still others 三段式 前文已经使用 Some place great emphasis on mechanical guarding. 和 Others stress safe work practices，本句是第三组并列，需要一个能与之衔接、表\"再有一些\"的词，正是英语固定三段式 Some... Others... Still others...。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Some 已在 Some place great emphasis on mechanical guarding. 出现，再用一次会造成第一组与第三组指代混淆，破坏并列对照。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Many 单用强调\"数量多\"，在 Some/Others 三段式里并不是地道的承接词，且会暗示\"大多数依赖情感诉求\"，超出原文论述的中性枚举。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Even 表\"甚至\"，会引入对前文的递进或意外性，但本段三组做法只是平行枚举，没有\"出乎意料\"的语气，逻辑色彩不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Still 与 others 构成 Still others，意为\"还有一些（人）\"，是 Some... Others... Still others... 三段式中的标准第三组承接，正与前两组并列衔接。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"comes off"},{"key":"B","text":"turns up"},{"key":"C","text":"pays off"},{"key":"D","text":"holds up"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"8.","reason":"From a financial standpoint alone 提示\"经济回报\" 本句状语 From a financial standpoint alone 已限定视角是\"仅从财务角度看\"，而下一句 The fewer the injury __(9)__, the better the workman's insurance rate. 又把视角具体落到\"伤害理赔越少，保险费率越好\"。两句联读，空格谓语必须表达\"安全 → 在财务上有回报/划算\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"comes off 意为\"成功；脱落\"，最多说计划\"奏效\"，但不强调\"在金钱上回本\"，与 From a financial standpoint alone 的视角不严丝合缝。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"turns up 意为\"出现、调高\"，与\"安全在财务上是回报\"的语义无关。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"pays off 是固定动词短语，意为\"（努力/投入）取得回报、得偿所愿\"，与 From a financial standpoint alone 的财务视角、以及后文用保险费率算账的逻辑完全契合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"holds up 意为\"支撑、经得起检验\"，多用于论点、结构是否站得住，不表达\"经济上划算\"。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"claims"},{"key":"B","text":"reports"},{"key":"C","text":"declarations"},{"key":"D","text":"proclamations"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"insurance rate 提示这是\"理赔\"语境 本句后半段 the better the workman's insurance rate 出现 insurance（保险），把整句锁定在工伤保险语境里——\"伤害+保险\"的固定搭配名词是 claims（理赔申请），即\"工伤理赔越少，保险费率越优\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"claims 在保险语境中特指\"理赔申请/索赔\"，injury claims 即工伤理赔，理赔越少→保险公司风险越低→ workman's insurance rate 越优，整条因果链完整。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"reports 意为\"报告\"，injury reports 是工伤事件报告，仅记录事件而未必涉及金钱赔付，与紧随其后的 insurance rate 之间的因果链不如 claims 直接。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"declarations 多指\"正式声明、申报\"，常用于海关、纳税、外交语境，不是英语保险行业指代\"理赔申请\"的标准词。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"proclamations 意为\"公告、宣告\"，多用于官方对公众宣布大政方针，与工伤理赔这种行政流程毫无关系。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"an advantage"},{"key":"B","text":"a benefit"},{"key":"C","text":"an interest"},{"key":"D","text":"a profit"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"or at a loss 锁定反义\"盈利\" 本句 This may mean the difference between operating at __(10)__ or at a loss. 中 or a loss 就是答案的最强线索：盈利—亏损是工商语境里固定的反义对，英语里与 at a loss 构成对照的固定表达就是 at a profit。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"an advantage 意为\"优势、有利条件\"，与\"亏损\"在维度上不对等——loss 谈财务结果，advantage 谈比较地位。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"a benefit 意为\"好处、收益\"，语义方向虽对，但英语里没有 operate at a benefit 这种说法，无法与 at a loss 构成固定反义对。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"an interest 在财务语境多指\"利息\"，在一般语境指\"兴趣、利益\"，不能直接与 loss 形成\"盈—亏\"对照。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"a profit 与 at 搭配成 at a profit\"盈利地\"，与 at a loss\"亏损地\"构成英语商业里固定的反义对，正回应 the difference between operating at __(10)__ or at a loss 这一对照框架。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Each of the passages below is followed by some questions. For each question there are four answers marked ［A］, ［B］, ［C］ and ［D］. Read the passages carefully and choose the best answer to each of the questions. Then mark your answer on ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets with a pencil. (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"It's a rough world out there. Step outside and you could break a leg slipping on your doormat. Light up the stove and you could burn down the house. Luckily, if the doormat or stove failed to warn of coming disaster, a successful lawsuit might compensate you for your troubles. Or so the thinking has gone since the early 1980s, when juries began holding more companies liable for their customers' misfortunes."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Feeling threatened, companies responded by writing ever-longer warning labels, trying to anticipate every possible accident. Today, stepladders carry labels several inches long that warn, among other things, that you might—surprise!—fall off. The label on a child's Batman cape cautions that the toy \"does not enable user to fly\"."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"While warnings are often appropriate and necessary—the dangers of drug interactions, for example—and many are required by state or federal regulations, it isn't clear that they actually protect the manufacturers and sellers from liability if a customer is injured. About 50 percent of the companies lose when injured customers take them to court."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Now the tide appears to be turning. As personal injury claims continue as before, some courts are beginning to side with defendants, especially in cases where a warning label probably wouldn't have changed anything. In May, Julie Nimmons, president of Schutt Sports in Illinois, successfully fought a lawsuit involving a football player who was paralyzed in a game while wearing a Schutt helmet. \"We're really sorry he has become paralyzed, but helmets aren't designed to prevent those kinds of injuries,\" says Nimmons. The jury agreed that the nature of the game, not the helmet, was the reason for the athlete's injury. At the same time, the American Law Institute—a group of judges, lawyers, and academics whose recommendations carry substantial weight—issued new guidelines for tort law stating that companies need not warn customers of obvious dangers or bombard them with a lengthy list of possible ones. \"Important information can get buried in a sea of trivialities,\" says a law professor at Cornell Law School who helped draft the new guidelines. If the moderate end of the legal community has its way, the information on products might actually be provided for the benefit of customers and not as protection against legal liability."}]},"questions":[{"n":11,"stem":"What were things like in 1980s when accidents happened?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Customers might be relieved of their disasters through lawsuits."},{"key":"B","text":"Injured customers could expect protection from the legal system."},{"key":"C","text":"Companies would avoid being sued by providing new warnings."},{"key":"D","text":"Juries tended to find fault with the compensations companies promised."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"1980年代发生事故时情况如何?","choicesZh":{"A":"顾客可能通过诉讼从灾难中得到补偿。","B":"受伤的顾客可以期待法律系统的保护。","C":"公司会通过提供新的警告来避免被起诉。","D":"陪审团倾向于认为公司承诺的赔偿有问题。"},"analysis":{"type":"What were things like in 1980s when accidents happened? 问的是某个具体时间段下事情是怎么样的，属于对原文某一处事实的提取。","parse":"题干 What were things like in 1980s when accidents happened? 主干是 What were things like，things like 是固定搭配，意为 things like = 情形如何；in 1980s when accidents happened 是介词短语加 when 定语从句，限定的是 1980s 这个时间段——即 \"事故发生时的 1980 年代是什么样子\"。结构平铺，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Luckily, if the doormat or stove failed to warn of coming disaster, a successful lawsuit might compensate you for your troubles. Or so the thinking has gone since the early 1980s, when juries began holding more companies liable for their customers' misfortunes.","locateZh":"幸运的是，如果门垫或炉子没能警示即将到来的灾祸，一场胜诉的官司或许还能补偿你的损失。至少自 1980 年代初起，人们就是这么想的——那时陪审团开始越来越多地判公司为顾客的不幸负责。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Customers might be relieved of their disasters through lawsuits 中的 relieved of their disasters 意为 \"灾难本身被解除/消除\"，而原文只说 compensate you for your troubles（事后获得赔偿）——灾难已经发生，无法被 \"relieved\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判说 \"顾客可以靠起诉获得保护\"，B 项 Injured customers could expect protection from the legal system 恰好以 legal system（司法系统）概括 juries（陪审团）的行为，是预判最自然的同义对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"juries began holding more companies liable for their customers' misfortunes","opt":"Injured customers could expect protection from the legal system"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Companies would avoid being sued by providing new warnings 描述的是公司写更多警告标签来防被告——这是第 2 段 Feeling threatened, companies responded by writing ever-longer warning labels 描述的 1980 年代之后公司的反应，而非 Q11 所问的 \"1980 年代事故发生时是什么样\" 的情形。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Juries tended to find fault with the compensations companies promised 称陪审团专挑公司补偿的毛病，但原文 juries began holding more companies liable 的意思是陪审团判公司承担责任、令其赔偿——立场正好相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":12,"stem":"Manufacturers as mentioned in the passage tend to____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"satisfy customers by writing long warnings on products"},{"key":"B","text":"become honest in describing the inadequacies of their products"},{"key":"C","text":"make the best use of labels to avoid legal liability"},{"key":"D","text":"feel obliged to view customers' safety as their first concern"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"文中提到的制造商倾向于____。","choicesZh":{"A":"通过在产品上写冗长的警告来满足顾客","B":"在描述其产品的不足之处时变得诚实","C":"充分利用标签来避免法律责任","D":"感到有义务将顾客的安全视为首要关切"},"analysis":{"type":"Manufacturers as mentioned in the passage tend to____ 是一句陈述句的延续，问的是文中提到的厂商常规倾向，属于一项明确事实的提取。","parse":"题干 Manufacturers as mentioned in the passage tend to____ 主干是 Manufacturers tend to____，as mentioned in the passage 是过去分词短语作后置定语，只起 \"文中提到的\" 这个限定作用；选项是 tend to 后面动词原形的延续。结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"Feeling threatened, companies responded by writing ever-longer warning labels, trying to anticipate every possible accident.","locateZh":"公司感到受到威胁，作出的反应是不断加长警告标签，试图预先标注每一种可能的事故。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"satisfy customers by writing long warnings on products 称厂商写长标签是为了 \"让顾客满意\"，但原文 Feeling threatened, companies responded 表明动机是公司自身害怕被告，与顾客满意无关。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"become honest in describing the inadequacies of their products 称厂商在描述产品缺陷上变得诚实，但原文只说他们在 trying to anticipate every possible accident 列举可能的事故，并未表达 \"诚实承认产品缺陷\" 这一褒义动机。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判同时强调 \"加长标签\" 和 \"自保\" 两个语义；C 项把这两点合并成 \"用足标签以避免法律责任\"，与定位句和邻段配合的目的完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"writing ever-longer warning labels, trying to anticipate every possible accident","opt":"make the best use of labels to avoid legal liability"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"feel obliged to view customers' safety as their first concern 称厂商感到有义务把顾客安全放首位，原文从未表达此意——相反，第 3 段还暗示警告并不能真正保护顾客；末段 If the moderate end of the legal community has its way, the information on products might actually be provided for the benefit of customers 用虚拟语气更说明 \"为顾客\" 尚未实现。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":13,"stem":"The case of Schutt helmet demonstrated that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"some injury claims were no longer supported by law"},{"key":"B","text":"helmets were not designed to prevent injuries"},{"key":"C","text":"product labels would eventually be discarded"},{"key":"D","text":"some sports games might lose popularity with athletes"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"Schutt头盔案例表明____。","choicesZh":{"A":"某些伤害索赔不再得到法律支持","B":"头盔并非设计用来预防伤害","C":"产品标签最终会被废弃","D":"某些体育比赛可能会失去运动员的欢迎"},"analysis":{"type":"The case of Schutt helmet demonstrated that____ 问案例\"证明了\"什么，问的是例子背后的论点而不是例子本身。","parse":"题干 The case of Schutt helmet demonstrated that____ 主干是 The case demonstrated that____，of Schutt helmet 是限定 case 的介词短语；that 引导的宾语从句的内容由四个选项分别补全。结构平铺，无陷阱。","locateEn":"As personal injury claims continue as before, some courts are beginning to side with defendants, especially in cases where a warning label probably wouldn't have changed anything. In May, Julie Nimmons, president of Schutt Sports in Illinois, successfully fought a lawsuit involving a football player who was paralyzed in a game while wearing a Schutt helmet.","locateZh":"尽管人身伤害索赔案件一如既往地增多，一些法庭开始倾向被告，尤其是在那些就算有警告标签也改变不了什么的案件中。五月份，伊利诺伊州 Schutt Sports 公司总裁 Julie Nimmons 成功打赢了一场官司，案件涉及一名在比赛中佩戴 Schutt 头盔而瘫痪的橄榄球运动员。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判说 \"某些索赔不再被支持\"，A 项 some injury claims were no longer supported by law 是该总括句的镜像同义改写，所以选 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"some courts are beginning to side with defendants","opt":"some injury claims were no longer supported by law"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"helmets were not designed to prevent injuries 复述的是案例当事人 Nimmons 的话 helmets aren't designed to prevent those kinds of injuries——这是案例的内部论据，不是案例所要论证的论点。例证目的题问的是论点，不是论据本身。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"product labels would eventually be discarded 称产品标签最终会被弃用，但原文末段只说 companies need not warn customers of obvious dangers or bombard them with a lengthy list of possible ones——只是不必再把警告写得又长又显而易见，并非整体弃用。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"some sports games might lose popularity with athletes 称某些体育项目可能不再受运动员欢迎，原文从未涉及运动员对项目的喜爱程度，只谈了比赛性质 the nature of the game 是受伤原因。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":14,"stem":"The author's attitude towards the issue seems to be____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"biased"},{"key":"B","text":"indifferent"},{"key":"C","text":"puzzling"},{"key":"D","text":"objective"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对这个问题的态度似乎是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"有偏见的","B":"漠不关心的","C":"令人困惑的","D":"客观的"},"analysis":{"type":"The author's attitude towards the issue seems to be____ 直接询问作者对该议题的整体态度。","parse":"题干 The author's attitude towards the issue seems to be____ 主干是 attitude seems to be____，towards the issue 是介词短语修饰 attitude；选项为表语形容词。结构平铺，无陷阱，但要注意 seems to be 的口气是 \"看起来似乎\"，提示答案多偏中性温和。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"biased 意为 \"有偏见的\"，与作者全文 While warnings are often appropriate and necessary 这种让步姿态矛盾——承认对方合理就是客观立场的标准信号，与 biased 互斥。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"indifferent 意为 \"漠不关心、无所谓\"，但作者花了四段详细展示双方论据，并明确表达对温和派的微倾向 If the moderate end of the legal community has its way——这都不是漠不关心的人会做的事。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"puzzling 意为 \"令人困惑的\"，是用来形容让别人感到困惑的事物，而非自己困惑的人；即便要表达作者本人的困惑，应该用 puzzled（被动感受）而非 puzzling（主动让别人困惑），故选项本身的搭配就不对路。即使勉强解释为 \"作者使别人困惑\"，全文论证清晰、立场温和，也并未让人困惑。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"让步从句 + 缓和动词 + 虚拟条件三种语法手段共同指向作者不偏不倚的客观立场；预判说 \"中立客观\"，D 项 objective 正好是该立场的标准用语。","pairs":[{"orig":"While warnings are often appropriate and necessary","opt":"objective"},{"orig":"Now the tide appears to be turning","opt":"objective"},{"orig":"If the moderate end of the legal community has its way, the information on products might actually be provided for the benefit of customers and not as protection against legal liability","opt":"objective"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"In the first year or so of Web business, most of the action has revolved around efforts to tap the consumer market. More recently, as the Web proved to be more than a fashion, companies have started to buy and sell products and services with one another. Such business to business sales make sense because business people typically know what product they're looking for."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"Nonetheless, many companies still hesitate to use the Web because of doubts about its reliability. \"Businesses need to feel they can trust the pathway between them and the supplier,\" says senior analyst Blane Erwin of Forrester Research. Some companies are limiting the risk by conducting online transactions only with established business partners who are given access to the company's private intranet."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"Another major shift in the model for Internet commerce concerns the technology available for marketing. Until recently, Internet marketing activities have focused on strategies to \"pull\" customers into sites. In the past year, however, software companies have developed tools that allow companies to \"push\" information directly out to consumers, transmitting marketing messages directly to targeted customers. Most notably, the Pointcast Network uses a screen saver to deliver a continually updated stream of news and advertisements to subscribers' computer monitors. Subscribers can customize the information they want to receive and proceed directly to a company's Web site. Companies such as Virtual Vineyards are already starting to use similar technologies to push messages to customers about special sales, product offerings, or other events. But push technology has earned the contempt of many Web users. Online culture thinks highly of the notion that the information flowing onto the screen comes there by specific request. Once commercial promotion begins to fill the screen uninvited, the distinction between the Web and television fades. That's a prospect that horrifies Net purists."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"But it is hardly inevitable that companies on the Web will need to resort to push strategies to make money. The examples of Virtual Vineyards, Amazon.com, and other pioneers show that a Web site selling the right kind of products with the right mix of interactivity, hospitality, and security will attract online customers. And the cost of computing power continues to free fall, which is a good sign for any enterprise setting up shop in silicon. People looking back 5 or 10 years from now may well wonder why so few companies took the online plunge."}]},"questions":[{"n":15,"stem":"We learn from the beginning of the passage that Web business____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has been striving to expand its market"},{"key":"B","text":"intended to follow a fanciful fashion"},{"key":"C","text":"tried but in vain to control the market"},{"key":"D","text":"has been booming for one year or so"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从文章开头我们了解到网络商业____。","choicesZh":{"A":"一直努力扩大其市场","B":"打算追随一种异想天开的时尚","C":"试图控制市场但徒劳无功","D":"已经蓬勃发展了一年左右"},"analysis":{"type":"We learn from the beginning of the passage that 是典型的从指定区域取客观信息的句式，不带 infer/imply 等推断信号词，所以走细节题路径。","parse":"Q15 主句是 We learn from the beginning of the passage that ____，that 引导的宾语从句正是空缺待补的部分，选项是这个宾语从句的整句。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"In the first year or so of Web business, most of the action has revolved around efforts to tap the consumer market.","locateZh":"在 Web 商务诞生头一年左右，绝大多数动作都围绕着想方设法打开消费者市场。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"选项 A 是对 efforts to tap the consumer market 的标准同义替换，与预判 \"一直在努力开拓市场\" 完全对位，因此锁定 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"efforts to tap the consumer market","opt":"striving to expand its market"},{"orig":"most of the action has revolved around","opt":"has been striving"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 intended to follow a fanciful fashion 把原文 as the Web proved to be more than a fashion（事实证明不止是潮流）这一对潮流的否定反向曲解为 \"打算追潮流\"，与原文极性相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说努力 tap the consumer market 与做 business to business sales，从未提及 \"控制市场\" 这一动作，也没有 in vain 的失败语义，整句属凭空捏造。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 In the first year or so of Web business, most of the action has revolved around 中 \"the first year or so\" 是修饰 Web business 起步阶段的时间范围，选项 has been booming for one year or so 把这一时间状语偷换成 \"已经繁荣了一年左右\" 的持续时段，且 booming 也是原文未出现的评价。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":16,"stem":"Speaking of the online technology available for marketing, the author implies that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the technology is popular with many Web users"},{"key":"B","text":"businesses have faith in the reliability of online transactions"},{"key":"C","text":"there is a radical change in strategy"},{"key":"D","text":"it is accessible limitedly to established partners"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"在谈到可用于营销的在线技术时,作者暗示____。","choicesZh":{"A":"该技术受到许多网络用户的欢迎","B":"企业对在线交易的可靠性有信心","C":"战略发生了根本性变化","D":"它只能有限地供既有合作伙伴使用"},"analysis":{"type":"the author implies that 中的 implies 是推断题的标志性动词，要求答案是定位句的合理一步延伸。","parse":"Q16 主句是 Speaking of ..., the author implies that ____。Speaking of 引导的是话题前置状语，that 后接宾语从句即选项；选项 C 的 there is 句型与 D 中的 it is accessible limitedly 句首代词 it 都需考生认清指代对象，但题干句法本身平铺直叙。","locateEn":"Another major shift in the model for Internet commerce concerns the technology available for marketing.","locateZh":"互联网商务模式的另一项重大转变与可用于营销的技术有关。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文末段 push technology has earned the contempt of many Web users 明确指出推送技术招致大量 Web 用户的鄙夷，与选项 popular with many Web users 表达的 \"广受欢迎\" 极性完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"businesses have faith in the reliability of online transactions 谈的是 \"对线上交易可靠性有信心\"，对应内容在 P2 的 doubts about its reliability——且原文是 doubts 而非 have faith，与本题问的 P3 营销技术段毫无关系。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项 C 是对定位句 Another major shift in the model for Internet commerce 的标准同义改写，且与紧随其后的 pull/push 对照逻辑完全自洽，与预判 \"策略发生根本变化\" 一致，因此锁定 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"Another major shift in the model for Internet commerce","opt":"a radical change in strategy"},{"orig":"strategies to \"pull\" customers into sites","opt":"a radical change in strategy"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"accessible limitedly to established partners 描述的是 P2 中 conducting online transactions only with established business partners 这一信任缓冲做法，与本题问的营销技术无关；同时主语 it 模糊，貌似指营销技术实际指企业内网，进一步偷换概念。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":17,"stem":"In the view of Net purists, ____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"there should be no marketing messages in online culture"},{"key":"B","text":"money making should be given priority to on the Web"},{"key":"C","text":"the Web should be able to function as the television set"},{"key":"D","text":"there should be no online commercial information without requests"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在网络纯粹主义者看来,____。","choicesZh":{"A":"在线文化中不应该有营销信息","B":"在网络上应该优先考虑赚钱","C":"网络应该能够像电视机一样发挥作用","D":"未经请求不应该有在线商业信息"},"analysis":{"type":"In the view of Net purists 要求查特定人群的观点，是典型的 \"谁说了什么\" 类细节题。","parse":"Q17 主句是 In the view of Net purists, ____，逗号后是待补的完整陈述句即选项；In the view of X 是介词短语作状语限定立场归属，结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"Online culture thinks highly of the notion that the information flowing onto the screen comes there by specific request. Once commercial promotion begins to fill the screen uninvited, the distinction between the Web and television fades. That's a prospect that horrifies Net purists.","locateZh":"网络文化高度推崇这样一种观念：屏幕上呈现的信息必须出自特定的请求。一旦商业推广不请自来地塞满屏幕，Web 与电视的界限就会消失。这正是让 Net 纯粹派感到恐惧的前景。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"no marketing messages in online culture 把 uninvited 这一限定条件扩大化为 \"任何 marketing messages 都不应出现\"，但原文只反对 \"不请自来\" 的商业推广，应用户请求送达的营销信息（如 Subscribers can customize the information they want to receive）并不被反对。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 P3 末 That's a prospect that horrifies Net purists 反映 Net purists 反感商业入侵；选项 money making should be given priority to on the Web 反而主张 Web 上应以赚钱为先，与他们立场极性完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文表明 Net purists 害怕的正是 the distinction between the Web and television fades——Web 像电视；选项 the Web should be able to function as the television set 反向主张 Web 应该具备电视功能，与原文立场恰好相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"选项 D 是对 Online culture thinks highly of the notion that the information flowing onto the screen comes there by specific request 的标准 \"无 X 无 Y\" 句型改写，恰好命中预判 \"信息必须基于用户请求\"，因此锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"the information flowing onto the screen comes there by specific request","opt":"there should be no online commercial information without requests"},{"orig":"commercial promotion begins to fill the screen uninvited","opt":"online commercial information"}]}}}}},{"n":18,"stem":"We learn from the last paragraph that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"pushing information on the Web is essential to Internet commerce"},{"key":"B","text":"interactivity, hospitality and security are important to online customers"},{"key":"C","text":"leading companies began to take the online plunge decades ago"},{"key":"D","text":"setting up shops in silicon is independent of the cost of computing power"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从最后一段我们了解到____。","choicesZh":{"A":"在网络上推送信息对互联网商业至关重要","B":"互动性、友好性和安全性对在线客户很重要","C":"领先公司几十年前就开始涉足在线领域","D":"在硅谷开店与计算能力的成本无关"},"analysis":{"type":"We learn from the last paragraph that 用 learn 而非 imply/infer，要求从末段取直接对应的信息，按细节题处理。","parse":"Q18 主句是 We learn from the last paragraph that ____，that 引导宾语从句即选项；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The examples of Virtual Vineyards, Amazon.com, and other pioneers show that a Web site selling the right kind of products with the right mix of interactivity, hospitality, and security will attract online customers.","locateZh":"Virtual Vineyards、Amazon.com 等先行者的例子表明：只要网站卖对的产品，并搭配恰当的互动性、贴心服务与安全保障，就能吸引在线顾客。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"末段首句 But it is hardly inevitable that companies on the Web will need to resort to push strategies to make money 明确否定 push 是必需手段；选项 pushing information on the Web is essential to Internet commerce 反向断言 push 必不可少，与原文极性完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 B 直接保留 interactivity, hospitality, and security 三个原词并把 will attract 改成评价句 are important to，与预判完全对位，因此锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"a Web site selling the right kind of products with the right mix of interactivity, hospitality, and security will attract online customers","opt":"interactivity, hospitality and security are important to online customers"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"末段 People looking back 5 or 10 years from now may well wonder why so few companies took the online plunge 是 \"未来回望现在\" 的视角，说明此时此刻入局者还很少；选项 leading companies began to take the online plunge decades ago 凭空把时间线挪到几十年前，是原文未出现的事实。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 the cost of computing power continues to free fall, which is a good sign for any enterprise setting up shop in silicon 明确指出在 silicon 上开店与算力成本紧密相关、是利好；选项 setting up shops in silicon is independent of the cost of computing power 反向说 \"与算力成本无关\"，与原文逻辑相反。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"An invisible border divides those arguing for computers in the classroom on the behalf of students' career prospects and those arguing for computers in the classroom for broader reasons of radical educational reform. Very few writers on the subject have explored this distinction—indeed, contradiction—which goes to the heart of what is wrong with the campaign to put computers in the classroom."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"An education that aims at getting a student a certain kind of job is a technical education, justified for reasons radically different from why education is universally required by law. It is not simply to raise everyone's job prospects that all children are legally required to attend school into their teens. Rather, we have a certain conception of the American citizen, a character who is incomplete if he cannot competently assess how his livelihood and happiness are affected by things outside of himself. But this was not always the case; before it was legally required for all children to attend school until a certain age, it was widely accepted that some were just not equipped by nature to pursue this kind of education. With optimism characteristic of all industrialized countries, we came to accept that everyone is fit to be educated. Computer-education advocates forsake this optimistic notion for a pessimism that betrays their otherwise cheery outlook. Banking on the confusion between educational and vocational reasons for bringing computers into schools, computer advocates often emphasize the job prospects of graduates over their educational achievement."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"There are some good arguments for a technical education given the right kind of student. Many European schools introduce the concept of professional training early on in order to make sure children are properly equipped for the professions they want to join. It is, however, presumptuous to insist that there will only be so many jobs for so many scientists, so many businessmen, so many accountants. Besides, this is unlikely to produce the needed number of every kind of professional in a country as large as ours and where the economy is spread over so many states and involves so many international corporations."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"But, for a small group of students, professional training might be the way to go since well-developed skills, all other factors being equal, can be the difference between having a job and not. Of course, the basics of using any computer these days are very simple. It does not take a lifelong acquaintance to pick up various software programs. If one wanted to become a computer engineer, that is, of course, an entirely different story. Basic computer skills take—at the very longest—a couple of months to learn. In any case, basic computer skills are only complementary to the host of real skills that are necessary to becoming any kind of professional. It should be observed, of course, that no school, vocational or not, is helped by a confusion over its purpose."}]},"questions":[{"n":19,"stem":"The author thinks the present rush to put computers in the classroom is____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"far reaching"},{"key":"B","text":"dubiously oriented"},{"key":"C","text":"self contradictory"},{"key":"D","text":"radically reformatory"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者认为目前急于将计算机引入课堂的做法是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"影响深远的","B":"导向可疑的","C":"自相矛盾的","D":"根本性改革的"},"analysis":{"type":"The author thinks the present rush to put computers in the classroom is 是典型的「the author thinks…is + 形容词」结构，问的是作者对一种现象的总评价。","parse":"Q19 是一个待补全的不完整陈述句，主干为 The author thinks (that) the present rush ... is ___；选项是 is 后的表语形容词。注意 the present rush to put computers in the classroom 整体是 thinks 的宾语从句主语，rush 是名词「热潮、一窝蜂」，不是动词。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"far reaching 指「影响深远」，但作者全篇都在质疑这场运动的立意，从未评价它「影响范围广」；原文 goes to the heart of what is wrong 是指「戳到要害」，不是「影响深远」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求负向评价 + 方向问题，选项 dubiously oriented 恰好同时满足负向（dubiously）与方向（oriented），与主线结论完全对位。","pairs":[{"orig":"contradiction—which goes to the heart of what is wrong with the campaign to put computers in the classroom","opt":"dubiously oriented"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"self contradictory 是「自身自相矛盾」，意指这件事是自我打脸的；但原文说的是 two groups of writers 之间存在 contradiction，即倡导者群体内部两类动机间的矛盾，不是 rush 本身的内在自相矛盾。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"radically reformatory 是「彻底改革式的」，来自原文 broader reasons of radical educational reform——那是被批评的一派人的口号，不是作者对这件事的评价；作者立场是负面，选 D 等于把批评对象的旗号当作者结论。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":20,"stem":"The belief that education is indispensable to all children____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is indicative of a pessimism in disguise"},{"key":"B","text":"came into being along with the arrival of computers"},{"key":"C","text":"is deeply rooted in the minds of computer-education"},{"key":"D","text":"originated from the optimistic attitude of industrialized countries"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"教育对所有儿童都不可或缺这一信念____。","choicesZh":{"A":"表明了一种变相的悲观主义","B":"随着计算机的出现而产生","C":"深深植根于计算机教育者的头脑中","D":"源于工业化国家的乐观态度"},"analysis":{"type":"The belief that education is indispensable to all children 已给定具体命题，问的是它的来源/性质，需要在原文中找出明确对应。","parse":"Q20 是不完整陈述句，主干是 The belief ... is / came / originated / 等动词；that education is indispensable to all children 是 belief 的同位语从句，限定 belief 的具体内容。indispensable to ≈ 对…不可或缺 ≈ 原文的 universally required / legally required。","locateEn":"With optimism characteristic of all industrialized countries, we came to accept that everyone is fit to be educated.","locateZh":"凭着所有工业化国家特有的乐观主义，我们逐渐接受了「每个人都适合接受教育」这种观念。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Computer-education advocates forsake this optimistic notion for a pessimism that betrays their otherwise cheery outlook 是说电脑教育倡导者藏着悲观，并不是说「education is indispensable」这一信念本身藏着悲观；选项把宿主对换了。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文明说 before it was legally required for all children to attend school until a certain age, it was widely accepted that some were just not equipped by nature——这种「人人都该受教育」的信念是在「立法强制义务教育」前后逐渐形成的，远早于电脑诞生；选项 B 说它与电脑同时出现，与时间链相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"is deeply rooted in the minds of computer-education 把信念落到 computer-education advocates 头上，但原文恰恰说倡导者 forsake this optimistic notion——他们抛弃了这种信念；选项与原文事实相反，且 minds of computer-education 短语本身残缺不完整。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求「信念源自工业化国家的乐观」，选项 D 在「源自」「乐观」「工业化国家」三处都与定位句对位。","pairs":[{"orig":"With optimism characteristic of all industrialized countries, we came to accept that everyone is fit to be educated","opt":"originated from the optimistic attitude of industrialized countries"}]}}}}},{"n":21,"stem":"It could be inferred from the passage that in the author's country the European model of professional training is____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"dependent upon the starting age of candidates"},{"key":"B","text":"worth trying in various social sections"},{"key":"C","text":"of little practical value"},{"key":"D","text":"attractive to every kind of professional"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从文中可以推断,在作者所在的国家,欧洲的职业培训模式是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"取决于候选人的起始年龄","B":"值得在各个社会部门尝试","C":"几乎没有实用价值","D":"对各类专业人士都有吸引力"},"analysis":{"type":"It could be inferred from the passage that 明确要求做推断，不是直接照搬原文。","parse":"Q21 是套了一层 it could be inferred from the passage that 的复合陈述句，主语从句为「the European model of professional training is ___」。is 后跟选项做表语；in the author's country 是介词短语状语，限定讨论域是作者本国，不是欧洲本土。","locateEn":"It is, however, presumptuous to insist that there will only be so many jobs for so many scientists, so many businessmen, so many accountants. Besides, this is unlikely to produce the needed number of every kind of professional in a country as large as ours and where the economy is spread over so many states and involves so many international corporations.","locateZh":"然而，硬说将来只会有这么多科学家、这么多商人、这么多会计师的岗位，未免太武断了。再说，在我们这样幅员辽阔、经济遍布众多州份、又牵涉众多跨国公司的国家，这种做法不太可能培养出所需数量的各类专业人才。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说 Many European schools introduce the concept of professional training early on，描述欧洲做法的时间安排，并未说这种模式的好坏「取决于」候选人的起始年龄；选项把描述性「早开始」偷换为条件性「取决于年龄」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文用 presumptuous + unlikely to produce 两次否定，明确该模式套到本国不可行；选项 worth trying in various social sections 反向给出积极建议，与作者立场完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"从 unlikely to produce 与 presumptuous 两个否定信号，一步推论可以得到「这种模式在本国实际价值不大」，正好对应 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"this is unlikely to produce the needed number of every kind of professional in a country as large as ours","opt":"of little practical value"},{"orig":"It is, however, presumptuous to insist that there will only be so many jobs for so many scientists, so many businessmen, so many accountants","opt":"of little practical value"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文恰恰说 this is unlikely to produce the needed number of every kind of professional——并不能产出各类专业人才所需数量；选项 attractive to every kind of professional 反过来说它对各类专业人士都有吸引力，方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"According to the author, basic computer skills should be____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"included as an auxiliary course in school"},{"key":"B","text":"highlighted in acquisition of professional qualifications"},{"key":"C","text":"mastered through a life-long course"},{"key":"D","text":"equally emphasized by any school, vocational or otherwise"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据作者的观点,计算机基本技能应该____。","choicesZh":{"A":"作为辅助课程纳入学校教育","B":"在获取职业资格时得到强调","C":"通过终身课程掌握","D":"受到任何学校的同等重视,无论是职业学校还是其他学校"},"analysis":{"type":"basic computer skills should be 锁定一个具体对象，要求复述作者对它的定性，可由末段定位句直接读出。","parse":"Q22 是不完整陈述句，主干是 basic computer skills should be ___；should be 后接选项作表语补足语。According to the author 是介词短语状语，再次强调立场归属是作者本人。","locateEn":"In any case, basic computer skills are only complementary to the host of real skills that are necessary to becoming any kind of professional.","locateZh":"不管怎么说，基本的计算机技能不过是成为任何一种专业人士所需的大量真正技能的辅助而已。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求「辅助性质」，选项 A 用 auxiliary course 承接 complementary、用 in school 承接末段对学校的回收，两端精准对位。","pairs":[{"orig":"basic computer skills are only complementary to the host of real skills","opt":"included as an auxiliary course in school"},{"orig":"no school, vocational or not, is helped by a confusion over its purpose","opt":"included as an auxiliary course in school"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 only complementary 明确把基础计算机技能压成「辅助」，选项 highlighted in acquisition of professional qualifications 反过来说要在获取专业资格时「重点强调」，方向完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文明说 It does not take a lifelong acquaintance to pick up various software programs 与 Basic computer skills take—at the very longest—a couple of months to learn，强调「两三个月就够」；选项 C 反过来说「需要终身课程」，与原文完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文末句 no school, vocational or not, is helped by a confusion over its purpose 说的是「不论是不是职业学校，搞乱目的都没好处」——主张「分清目的」；选项 equally emphasized by any school, vocational or otherwise 偷换为「任何学校都应同等强调电脑技能」，从「分清目的」滑到了「不分目的同等对待」，与原文方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"When a Scottish research team startled the world by revealing 3 months ago that it had cloned an adult sheep, President Clinton moved swiftly. Declaring that he was opposed to using this unusual animal husbandry technique to clone humans, he ordered that federal funds not be used for such an experiment—although no one had proposed to do so—and asked an independent panel of experts chaired by Princeton President Harold Shapiro to report back to the White House in 90 days with recommendations for a national policy on human cloning. That group—the National Bioethics Advisory Commission (NBAC)—has been working feverishly to put its wisdom on paper, and at a meeting on 17 May, members agreed on a near final draft of their recommendations."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"NBAC will ask that Clinton's 90-day ban on federal funds for human cloning be extended indefinitely, and possibly that it be made law. But NBAC members are planning to word the recommendation narrowly to avoid new restrictions on research that involves the cloning of human DNA or cells—routine in molecular biology. The panel has not yet reached agreement on a crucial question, however, whether to recommend legislation that would make it a crime for private funding to be used for human cloning."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"In a draft preface to the recommendations, discussed at the 17 May meeting, Shapiro suggested that the panel had found a broad consensus that it would be \"morally unacceptable to attempt to create a human child by adult nuclear cloning.\" Shapiro explained during the meeting that the moral doubt stems mainly from fears about the risk to the health of the child. The panel then informally accepted several general conclusions, although some details have not been settled."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"NBAC plans to call for a continued ban on federal government funding for any attempt to clone body cell nuclei to create a child. Because current federal law already forbids the use of federal funds to create embryos (the earliest stage of human offspring before birth) for research or to knowingly endanger an embryo's life, NBAC will remain silent on embryo research."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"NBAC members also indicated that they would appeal to privately funded researchers and clinics not to try to clone humans by body cell nuclear transfer. But they were divided on whether to go further by calling for a federal law that would impose a complete ban on human cloning. Shapiro and most members favored an appeal for such legislation, but in a phone interview, he said this issue was still \"up in the air\"."}]},"questions":[{"n":23,"stem":"We can learn from the first paragraph that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"federal funds have been used in a project to clone humans"},{"key":"B","text":"the White House responded strongly to the news of cloning"},{"key":"C","text":"NBAC was authorized to control the misuse of cloning technique"},{"key":"D","text":"the White House has got the panel's recommendations on cloning"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从第一段我们可以得知____。","choicesZh":{"A":"联邦资金已被用于克隆人类的项目","B":"白宫对克隆消息作出了强烈回应","C":"NBAC被授权控制克隆技术的滥用","D":"白宫已收到专家组关于克隆的建议"},"analysis":{"type":"We can learn from the first paragraph that 句式是\"从某段我们得知\"，要求把选项回贴到首段做事实核对，并无 infer/imply/suggest 这类推断信号。","parse":"We can learn from the first paragraph that____ 是一个待补全的陈述句，主句 We can learn 后接 from 介词短语限定信息出处，that 后留白等选项补成宾语从句；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"When a Scottish research team startled the world by revealing 3 months ago that it had cloned an adult sheep, President Clinton moved swiftly. Declaring that he was opposed to using this unusual animal husbandry technique to clone humans, he ordered that federal funds not be used for such an experiment—although no one had proposed to do so—and asked an independent panel of experts chaired by Princeton President Harold Shapiro to report back to the White House in 90 days with recommendations for a national policy on human cloning.","locateZh":"当苏格兰研究团队 3 个月前披露其克隆出一只成年绵羊、震惊世界时，克林顿总统迅速行动：他声明反对将这种不寻常的畜牧技术用于克隆人，下令联邦资金不得用于此类实验——尽管尚无人提议做此事——并委派由普林斯顿校长 Harold Shapiro 主持的独立专家组在 90 天内就克隆人国家政策向白宫提交建议。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文明说 although no one had proposed to do so——根本没人提议过克隆人，更不可能已有联邦资金被用过；选项 federal funds have been used in a project to clone humans 正好与原文事实相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判结论\"白宫反应强烈迅速\"和 the White House responded strongly to the news of cloning 在主语、动作、对象上一一对应，无需二次推理。","pairs":[{"orig":"President Clinton moved swiftly","opt":"the White House responded strongly to the news of cloning"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文交给 NBAC 的任务是 report back to the White House in 90 days with recommendations for a national policy on human cloning——提建议，而非 control the misuse of cloning technique——管控滥用；后者把咨询职能偷换成执法职能。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"首段说 NBAC has been working feverishly to put its wisdom on paper、5 月 17 日才 agreed on a near final draft——还在写、是\"近终稿\"，根本没递交白宫；选项 the White House has got the panel's recommendations on cloning 说白宫\"已拿到\"建议，与事实相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"The panel agreed on all of the following except that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the ban on federal funds for human cloning should be made a law"},{"key":"B","text":"the cloning of human DNA is not to be put under more control"},{"key":"C","text":"it is criminal to use private funding for human cloning"},{"key":"D","text":"it would be against ethical values to clone a human being"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"专家组在以下所有方面达成一致，除了____。","choicesZh":{"A":"禁止将联邦资金用于克隆人类应成为一项法律","B":"克隆人类DNA不应受到更多控制","C":"使用私人资金进行克隆人类属于犯罪行为","D":"克隆人类将违背伦理价值观"},"analysis":{"type":"agreed on all of the following except 要求每个选项都能或不能在原文找到事实对应，是典型的细节核对任务。","parse":"The panel agreed on all of the following except that____ 主干 The panel agreed on X，except that 引导排除分句，that 后留白；隐含逻辑是\"panel agreed on A、B、D，但 panel did NOT agree on 答案项\"——读题时一定把 except 在脑里展开成否定，否则容易看反。","locateEn":"NBAC will ask that Clinton's 90-day ban on federal funds for human cloning be extended indefinitely, and possibly that it be made law. But NBAC members are planning to word the recommendation narrowly to avoid new restrictions on research that involves the cloning of human DNA or cells—routine in molecular biology. The panel has not yet reached agreement on a crucial question, however, whether to recommend legislation that would make it a crime for private funding to be used for human cloning.","locateZh":"NBAC 将申请把克林顿 90 天的联邦资金克隆人禁令无限期延长，并可能提议把它写入法律；但 NBAC 成员计划将建议措辞收窄，以避免对涉及人 DNA 或细胞的克隆研究（分子生物学常规操作）施加新限制；然而专家组在一个关键问题上 has not yet reached agreement：是否建议立法把私人资金用于克隆人的行为定罪。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"NBAC will ask that Clinton's 90-day ban on federal funds for human cloning be extended indefinitely, and possibly that it be made law 明确说 panel 将提议把 90 天禁令延长并可能立法，这与 the ban on federal funds for human cloning should be made a law 一致——属于 panel agreed on 的项，不是答案。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"NBAC members are planning to word the recommendation narrowly to avoid new restrictions on research that involves the cloning of human DNA or cells 明确说要避免对 DNA/细胞克隆施加新限制——正与 the cloning of human DNA is not to be put under more control 同义，属于已达成的项。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"A、B、D 在 P2 与 P3 都能找到\"panel 已达成\"的明确出处，唯独 C 在 P2 被明确写为 has not yet reached agreement，正是 except 所要的那一项。","pairs":[{"orig":"The panel has not yet reached agreement on a crucial question, however, whether to recommend legislation that would make it a crime for private funding to be used for human cloning","opt":"it is criminal to use private funding for human cloning"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the panel had found a broad consensus that it would be \"morally unacceptable to attempt to create a human child by adult nuclear cloning\" 明确说 panel 在伦理上达成共识，与 it would be against ethical values to clone a human being 同义，属于已达成的项。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"NBAC will leave the issue of embryo research undiscussed because____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"embryo research is just a current development of cloning"},{"key":"B","text":"the health of the child is not the main concern of embryo research"},{"key":"C","text":"an embryo's life will not be endangered in embryo research"},{"key":"D","text":"the issue is explicitly stated and settled in the law"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"NBAC将不讨论胚胎研究问题,因为____。","choicesZh":{"A":"胚胎研究只是克隆技术当前的一个发展方向","B":"儿童的健康不是胚胎研究的主要关注点","C":"胚胎研究中胚胎的生命不会受到威胁","D":"该问题在法律中已明确阐述并得到解决"},"analysis":{"type":"NBAC will leave the issue of embryo research undiscussed because 问的是原文已经给出的原因，不需要二度推理。","parse":"NBAC will leave the issue of embryo research undiscussed because____ leave + 宾语 + 形容词补语\"使……保持……状态\"，相当于 will not discuss the issue；because 引导原因状语从句，答案补完整 because 后的内容；注意 leave...undiscussed 这个搭配考生易看漏 un- 前缀而误读为\"将讨论\"。","locateEn":"Because current federal law already forbids the use of federal funds to create embryos (the earliest stage of human offspring before birth) for research or to knowingly endanger an embryo's life, NBAC will remain silent on embryo research.","locateZh":"因为现行联邦法律已经禁止用联邦资金来创造胚胎（人类出生前最早期阶段）以供研究、或故意危害胚胎生命，所以 NBAC 将对胚胎研究问题保持沉默。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未把胚胎研究称作\"克隆的当前发展\"；embryo research is just a current development of cloning 用\"current development of cloning\"挂钩文章主题词\"克隆\"来诱导，但 P4 的因果链与此无关。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the moral doubt stems mainly from fears about the risk to the health of the child 是 panel 对克隆人的伦理担忧的解释，并非 NBAC 不讨论胚胎研究的原因；the health of the child is not the main concern of embryo research 把 P3 的论据搬到 P4 的问题上。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文说现行联邦法 forbids...to knowingly endanger an embryo's life——也就是\"禁止故意危及胚胎生命\"，但禁令只覆盖\"用联邦资金的故意危害\"；选项 an embryo's life will not be endangered in embryo research 直接断言胚胎在胚胎研究中不会被危害，把\"被法律禁止\"偷换成\"不会发生\"，与原文的事实性禁止状态不符。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"联邦法已明禁不必再议\"和 the issue is explicitly stated and settled in the law 完全对应——法律已经说清并搞定，所以 NBAC 在这事上无需再发声。","pairs":[{"orig":"Because current federal law already forbids the use of federal funds to create embryos (the earliest stage of human offspring before birth) for research or to knowingly endanger an embryo's life","opt":"the issue is explicitly stated and settled in the law"}]}}}}},{"n":26,"stem":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"some NBAC members hesitate to ban human cloning completely"},{"key":"B","text":"a law banning human cloning is to be passed in no time"},{"key":"C","text":"privately funded researchers will respond positively to NBAC's appeal"},{"key":"D","text":"the issue of human cloning will soon be settled"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从最后一段可以推断出____。","choicesZh":{"A":"一些NBAC成员对完全禁止克隆人类持犹豫态度","B":"禁止克隆人类的法律将立即通过","C":"私人资助的研究人员将积极回应NBAC的呼吁","D":"克隆人类的问题将很快得到解决"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that 的 inferred 是推断题最显性的标志词。","parse":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that____ 形式主语 It + 被动 can be inferred from + 来源，that 后留白等待选项补成主语从句的真实主语；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱，关键只在抓住 inferred 这个题型信号。","locateEn":"But they were divided on whether to go further by calling for a federal law that would impose a complete ban on human cloning. Shapiro and most members favored an appeal for such legislation, but in a phone interview, he said this issue was still \"up in the air\".","locateZh":"但他们在\"是否进一步呼吁联邦立法以全面禁止克隆人\"上 were divided；Shapiro 与多数成员支持发起这样的立法呼吁，但他在电话采访中说，此事仍 up in the air（悬而未决）。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文\"成员们在是否进一步推全面禁止上分裂\"和\"Shapiro 多数支持但 up in the air\"，自然延伸出\"部分成员对完整禁止仍犹豫\"——正是 some NBAC members hesitate to ban human cloning completely。","pairs":[{"orig":"they were divided on whether to go further by calling for a federal law that would impose a complete ban on human cloning","opt":"some NBAC members hesitate to ban human cloning completely"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文明说此事 up in the air——悬而未决，没有任何迹象表明法律将\"即刻\"通过；选项 a law banning human cloning is to be passed in no time 把分裂未决直接说成\"立法马上通过\"，与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说 NBAC would appeal to privately funded researchers and clinics not to try to clone humans——发出呼吁；至于私人资助方会不会\"正面响应\"，原文一字未提；privately funded researchers will respond positively to NBAC's appeal 等于替私人资助方表态。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 up in the air 明示此事悬而未决，没有任何时间表；the issue of human cloning will soon be settled 与之相反，把\"悬未决\"硬推成\"很快搞定\"。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-5","kind":"reading","title":"Text 5","textNo":5,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 5","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-1","text":"Science, in practice, depends far less on the experiments it prepares than on the preparedness of the minds of the men who watch the experiments. Sir Isaac Newton supposedly discovered gravity through the fall of an apple. Apples had been falling in many places for centuries and thousands of people had seen them fall. But Newton for years had been curious about the cause of the orbital motion of the moon and planets. What kept them in place? Why didn't they fall out of the sky? The fact that the apple fell down toward the earth and not up into the tree answered the question he had been asking himself about those larger fruits of the heavens, the moon and the planets."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-2","text":"How many men would have considered the possibility of an apple falling up into the tree? Newton did because he was not trying to predict anything. He was just wondering. His mind was ready for the unpredictable. Unpredictability is part of the essential nature of research. If you don't have unpredictable things, you don't have research. Scientists tend to forget this when writing their cut and dried reports for the technical journals, but history is filled with examples of it."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-3","text":"In talking to some scientists, particularly younger ones, you might gather the impression that they find the \"scientific method\" a substitute for imaginative thought. I've attended research conferences where a scientist has been asked what he thinks about the advisability of continuing a certain experiment. The scientist has frowned, looked at the graphs, and said, \"the data are still inconclusive.\" \"We know that,\" the men from the budget office have said, \"but what do you think? Is it worthwhile going on? What do you think we might expect?\" The scientist has been shocked at having even been asked to speculate."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-4","text":"What this amounts to, of course, is that the scientist has become the victim of his own writings. He has put forward unquestioned claims so consistently that he not only believes them himself, but has convinced industrial and business management that they are true. If experiments are planned and carried out according to plan as faithfully as the reports in the science journals indicate, then it is perfectly logical for management to expect research to produce results measurable in dollars and cents. It is entirely reasonable for auditors to believe that scientists who know exactly where they are going and how they will get there should not be distracted by the necessity of keeping one eye on the cash register while the other eye is on the microscope. Nor, if regularity and conformity to a standard pattern are as desirable to the scientist as the writing of his papers would appear to reflect, is management to be blamed for discriminating against the \"odd balls\" among researchers in favor of more conventional thinkers who \"work well with the team\"."}]},"questions":[{"n":27,"stem":"The author wants to prove with the example of Isaac Newton that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"inquiring minds are more important than scientific experiments"},{"key":"B","text":"science advances when fruitful researches are conducted"},{"key":"C","text":"scientists seldom forget the essential nature of research"},{"key":"D","text":"unpredictability weighs less than prediction in scientific research"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者想通过 Isaac Newton 的例子来证明____。","choicesZh":{"A":"探究精神比科学实验更重要","B":"当进行富有成果的研究时科学就会进步","C":"科学家很少忘记研究的本质","D":"在科学研究中不可预测性不如预测重要"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The author wants to prove with the example of Isaac Newton that 明确问举例的目的，是典型的例证目的题特征。","parse":"主干是 The author wants to prove ... that____，that 引导宾语从句作 prove 的宾语，空格填的是从句内容；with the example of Isaac Newton 是方式状语，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Science, in practice, depends far less on the experiments it prepares than on the preparedness of the minds of the men who watch the experiments.","locateZh":"在实践中，科学的进步远不依赖于它所设计的实验本身，而是依赖于那些观察实验的人是否拥有有准备的头脑。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项把段首论点句的两端（inquiring minds 对应 preparedness of the minds，scientific experiments 对应 experiments it prepares）以同样的比较结构呈现，正是预判的等价表达。","pairs":[{"orig":"the preparedness of the minds of the men who watch the experiments","opt":"inquiring minds"},{"orig":"depends far less on the experiments it prepares than on the preparedness of the minds","opt":"are more important than scientific experiments"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"science advances when fruitful researches are conducted 把作者论点偷换成\"只要做了富有成果的研究，科学就进步\"，跟原文\"靠头脑有准备\"完全是两条因果链；牛顿例子里成功的不是\"做了多少实验\"，而是\"带着疑问观察\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项说 scientists seldom forget the essential nature of research——科学家很少忘掉研究的本质；但 P2 明确说 Scientists tend to forget this，方向完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"unpredictability weighs less than prediction in scientific research 凭空在 unpredictability 和 prediction 之间制造一个轻重比较，原文虽提到 Unpredictability is part of the essential nature of research，但根本未与 prediction 做\"轻重\"对比，更何况方向也与作者真实立场相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"The author asserts that scientists____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"shouldn't replace \"scientific method\" with imaginative thought"},{"key":"B","text":"shouldn't neglect to speculate on unpredictable things"},{"key":"C","text":"should write more concise reports for technical journals"},{"key":"D","text":"should be confident about their research findings"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者断言科学家____。","choicesZh":{"A":"不应该用想象性思维取代\"科学方法\"","B":"不应该忽视对不可预测事物的思考","C":"应该为技术期刊撰写更简明的报告","D":"应该对自己的研究发现充满信心"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The author asserts that 问的是作者直接说了什么，不要求推断，是细节题中的作者观点直陈类。","parse":"The author asserts that____ 中 that 引导宾语从句作 asserts 的宾语，空格补全的是宾语从句的内容；句式简单，无修饰陷阱。","locateEn":"Unpredictability is part of the essential nature of research. If you don't have unpredictable things, you don't have research. Scientists tend to forget this when writing their cut and dried reports for the technical journals, but history is filled with examples of it.","locateZh":"不可预测性是研究本质的一部分。没有不可预测的事，就没有研究。科学家在为专业期刊写那些井井有条的报告时容易忘了这一点，但历史上充满了这样的例子。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"shouldn't replace \"scientific method\" with imaginative thought 反了：原文 they find the \"scientific method\" a substitute for imaginative thought 批评的是科学家用\"科学方法\"取代想象力——作者其实希望多一点想象力，而不是相反；A 项却让科学家不要用想象力取代科学方法，完全颠倒。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项把\"科学家容易忘记不可预测性\"这一作者负面评价转为\"科学家不该忽视对不可预测之事的推测\"，方向与作者立场一致，覆盖了定位句的核心。","pairs":[{"orig":"Scientists tend to forget this","opt":"shouldn't neglect to speculate on unpredictable things"},{"orig":"Unpredictability is part of the essential nature of research","opt":"speculate on unpredictable things"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未让科学家写得 more concise，只批评他们写得 cut and dried（千篇一律、过于工整）；concise 是\"简明\"，与 cut and dried 不同语义场，是凭空建议。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"should be confident about their research findings 让科学家对自己的研究发现更自信——但作者整篇都在批评科学家过度自信、把不确定的东西写得井井有条；让他们再更自信，与作者立场完全相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"It seems that some young scientists____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have a keen interest in prediction"},{"key":"B","text":"often speculate on the future"},{"key":"C","text":"think highly of creative thinking"},{"key":"D","text":"stick to \"scientific method\""}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"看起来一些年轻科学家____。","choicesZh":{"A":"对预测有浓厚兴趣","B":"经常推测未来","C":"高度评价创造性思维","D":"坚持\"科学方法\""},"analysis":{"type":"题干 It seems that some young scientists 用 seems 表示作者并非直陈而是引出推论，是典型推断题信号。","parse":"It seems that some young scientists____ 是 It seems that 引导的主语从句结构，空格补的是 that 从句中科学家做什么；some 限定 young scientists，注意\"部分\"含义，不要扩为全部。","locateEn":"In talking to some scientists, particularly younger ones, you might gather the impression that they find the \"scientific method\" a substitute for imaginative thought. ... The scientist has been shocked at having even been asked to speculate.","locateZh":"在与一些科学家——尤其是年轻一辈——交谈时，你可能会产生这样的印象：他们把\"科学方法\"视作富有想象力的思考的替代品。……科学家对仅仅是被要求做推测都感到震惊。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"have a keen interest in prediction 说年轻科学家对预测有浓厚兴趣，但原文 The scientist has been shocked at having even been asked to speculate 表明他们对推测/预测避之不及，立场完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"often speculate on the future 说他们经常推测未来，但原文反复显示他们一被要求 speculate 就 shocked，是相反的群体行为。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"think highly of creative thinking 说他们高度推崇创造性思维，但原文明说他们把\"科学方法\"当作 a substitute for imaginative thought——用流程取代想象，正是不推崇想象/创造性思维。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"当\"科学方法\"被当作\"想象\"的替代，意味着他们只用\"科学方法\"，正是 stick to 的含义；再结合段末 shocked at having even been asked to speculate 进一步坐实。","pairs":[{"orig":"they find the \"scientific method\" a substitute for imaginative thought","opt":"stick to \"scientific method\""},{"orig":"the data are still inconclusive","opt":"stick to \"scientific method\""}]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"The author implies that the results of scientific research____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"may not be as profitable as they are expected"},{"key":"B","text":"can be measured in dollars and cents"},{"key":"C","text":"rely on conformity to a standard pattern"},{"key":"D","text":"are mostly underestimated by management"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"作者暗示科学研究的成果____。","choicesZh":{"A":"可能不像预期的那样有价值","B":"可以用金钱来衡量","C":"依赖于对标准模式的遵循","D":"大多被管理层低估"},"analysis":{"type":"The author implies that the results of scientific research____ 中 implies 是推断题的硬信号，要求从字面背后读出作者立场。","parse":"The author implies that the results of scientific research____ 中 that 引导宾语从句，空格补的是从句谓语部分；the results of scientific research 是从句主语，注意作者用的是 implies 而非 says——答案不在字面而在弦外之音。","locateEn":"If experiments are planned and carried out according to plan as faithfully as the reports in the science journals indicate, then it is perfectly logical for management to expect research to produce results measurable in dollars and cents.","locateZh":"如果实验真像科学期刊上的报告所暗示的那样，按计划被忠实地设计和实施，那么管理层期望研究能产出可以用金钱衡量的成果，就完全合乎逻辑。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"作者把 results measurable in dollars and cents 写成管理层\"合乎逻辑\"的期望，本意是讽刺它建立在错误前提上；故作者实际暗示是 may not be as profitable as they are expected。","pairs":[{"orig":"research to produce results measurable in dollars and cents","opt":"may not be as profitable as they are expected"},{"orig":"Unpredictability is part of the essential nature of research","opt":"may not be as profitable as they are expected"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"can be measured in dollars and cents 直接把原文反讽的话当作作者主张照搬，可衡量正是被作者讽刺的天真期望，不是作者真实立场。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"rely on conformity to a standard pattern 说科研结果依赖于\"墨守成规\"——但原文 regularity and conformity to a standard pattern 描述的是\"科学家写论文呈现的姿态\"，并非科研结果本身依赖于此；把\"写作风格\"算到\"结果\"头上是张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"are mostly underestimated by management 说成果\"大多被管理层低估\"，但原文相反——管理层是被科学家自己骗得期望过高（has convinced industrial and business management that they are true），是\"高估\"而非\"低估\"。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","text":"(31) While there are almost as many definitions of history as there are historians, modern practice most closely conforms to one that sees history as the attempt to recreate and explain the significant events of the past. Caught in the web of its own time and place, each generation of historians determines anew what is significant for it in the past. In this search the evidence found is always incomplete and scattered; it is also frequently partial or partisan. The irony of the historian's craft is that its practitioners always know that their efforts are but contributions to an unending process."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","text":"(32) Interest in historical methods has arisen less through external challenge to the validity of history as an intellectual discipline and more from internal quarrels among historians themselves. While history once revered its affinity to literature and philosophy, the emerging social sciences seemed to afford greater opportunities for asking new questions and providing rewarding approaches to an understanding of the past. Social science methodologies had to be adapted to a discipline governed by the primacy of historical sources rather than the imperatives of the contemporary world. (33) During this transfer, traditional historical methods were augmented by additional methodologies designed to interpret the new forms of evidence in the historical study."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","text":"Methodology is a term that remains inherently ambiguous in the historical profession. (34) There is no agreement whether methodology refers to the concepts peculiar to historical work in general or to the research techniques appropriate to the various branches of historical inquiry. Historians, especially those so blinded by their research interests that they have been accused of \"tunnel method,\" frequently fall victim to the \"technical fallacy.\" Also common in the natural sciences, the technicist fallacy mistakenly identifies the discipline as a whole with certain parts of its technical implementation."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","text":"(35) It applies equally to traditional historians who view history as only the external and internal criticism of sources, and to social science historians who equate their activity with specific techniques."}]},"sentences":[{"n":31,"en":"While there are almost as many definitions of history as there are historians, modern practice most closely conforms to one that sees history as the attempt to recreate and explain the significant events of the past.","refZh":"尽管几乎有多少位史学家，就有多少种关于历史学的定义，但现代史学实践最为符合这样一种定义：它把历史学视为对过去重大事件加以重建和解释的一种努力。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"While there are almost as many definitions of history as there are historians,","lit":"尽管几乎有多少历史学家就有多少种历史学的定义，","role":"（While 引导的让步状语从句（内嵌 as...as 同级比较））","note":"难点： as many ... as 同级比较 + while 让步 难点一：while 在这里不是\"当……时\"，而是\"尽管/虽然\"的让步连词（看后半句出现转折语气即可判定）。难点二：as many definitions of history as there are historians 是\"as 形容词/名词 as\"的同级比较结构，字面是\"几乎和史学家一样多的历史学定义\"，地道汉化为\"几乎有多少位史学家，就有多少种历史学的定义\"。"},{"en":"modern practice most closely conforms to one","lit":"现代（史学）实践最为接近一种（定义）","role":"（主句主干（主谓宾））","note":"难点： one 的回指还原 + conform to 的取义 one 不能译成\"一个\"，要回上文还原为 one definition——即\"一种定义\"。conform to 在此不是\"遵守（规则）\"，而是\"与……相符/接近\"，对应 as many definitions ... modern practice most closely conforms to one 的语境，宜译为\"最接近/最符合\"。"},{"en":"that sees history as the attempt to recreate and explain the significant events of the past.","lit":"（这种定义）把历史看作重建并解释过去重大事件的尝试。","role":"（that 引导的定语从句，修饰 one）","note":"难点： see A as B + 抽象名词 attempt 具体化 see ... as ... 是固定结构，意为\"把……看作/视为……\"。attempt 是抽象名词，直译\"尝试\"偏生硬，建议在句中具体化为\"努力\"或干脆动词化为\"力图……\"。recreate 此处不是\"娱乐\"的熟义，而是\"重建/再现\"——配合 events of the past 的语境，僻义反而是常用义。"}]},{"n":32,"en":"Interest in historical methods has arisen less through external challenge to the validity of history as an intellectual discipline and more from internal quarrels among historians themselves.","refZh":"人们之所以对历史研究方法产生兴趣，与其说是因为外界对历史学作为一门知识学科的合理性提出了挑战，不如说是因为史学家们内部自己发生了争论。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Interest in historical methods has arisen","lit":"对历史研究方法的兴趣兴起（产生）","role":"（主干（主语 + 谓语））","note":"难点： 抽象主语 + 现在完成时的动词化 Interest 作主语是抽象名词，直译\"兴趣已经产生\"偏生硬。主体考生可把抽象名词\"反具体化\"为动词搭配：\"人们对……产生了兴趣\"或\"对……的兴趣之所以兴起\"，让中文读起来像句子而不是名词堆叠。"},{"en":"less through external challenge to the validity of history as an intellectual discipline","lit":"更少地源自对历史学作为一门知识学科的有效性的外部挑战，","role":"（方式状语（less through... 与下文 more from... 构成 less...more... 比较））","note":"难点： less ... and more ... 比较结构 + as 引导的同位关系 难点一：less ... more ... 不是\"较少……较多……\"的程度词，而是\"与其说……不如说……\"的比较框架，必须整体处理才地道。难点二：history as an intellectual discipline 中的 as 是\"作为\"的同位关系，整组译为\"历史学作为一门知识学科\"——validity 在此取\"合理性/正当性\"而非\"有效性\"，是熟词僻义。"},{"en":"and more from internal quarrels among historians themselves.","lit":"（而）更多地源自史学家们内部的争论。","role":"（方式状语（与上文 less through... 并列））","note":"难点： quarrel 的语境化 + themselves 的强调 quarrel 字面是\"吵架\"，学术语境中宜软化为\"争论/分歧\"；historians themselves 中 themselves 是反身代词强调，译为\"史学家们自身/史学家们内部\"，与上文的 external（外部）形成对照。"}]},{"n":33,"en":"During this transfer, traditional historical methods were augmented by additional methodologies designed to interpret the new forms of evidence in the historical study.","refZh":"在这种（社会科学方法向历史学的）转换过程中，传统的历史研究方法又得到了新增方法论的补充，这些新方法论旨在解释历史研究中出现的新型证据形式。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"During this transfer,","lit":"在这次转换过程中，","role":"（时间状语 + 跨句指代）","note":"难点： this transfer 必须回上文还原 this transfer 是跨段指代，孤立译成\"这次转换\"会让中文读者完全摸不着头脑。回上文 Social science methodologies had to be adapted to a discipline governed by the primacy of historical sources 可知 transfer 指\"把社会科学方法引入/移植到历史学研究的过程\"。翻译时要把这层显化出来，译成\"在这种（社会科学方法向历史学的）引入过程中\"或至少加上\"这种\"二字定位。"},{"en":"traditional historical methods were augmented by additional methodologies","lit":"传统的历史研究方法被新增的方法论（所）补充/扩充","role":"（主干（被动语态））","note":"难点： 被动语态转主动 + augment 的取义 augment 是\"增加、扩充、补充\"，比 add 正式，学术写作里高频。were augmented by 是典型被动，汉语不宜直留\"被……\"，按\"汉语少用被动\"原则改成\"X 又得到 Y 的扩充\"或\"在 X 之上又增添了 Y\"。methods 与 methodologies 在本句要做区分：methods=具体的\"研究方法\"，methodologies=更宏观的\"方法论\"——译文上要让它们看起来不一样。"},{"en":"designed to interpret the new forms of evidence in the historical study.","lit":"（这些方法论）旨在解释历史研究中新出现的证据形式。","role":"（过去分词短语作后置定语，修饰 methodologies）","note":"难点： designed to 的后置定语处理 + new forms of evidence 的取义 designed to do 在这里不是\"被设计来\"，而是\"旨在……\"或\"用以……\"——主体考生常硬译成\"被设计的\"，读起来像翻译软件。new forms of evidence 指的是\"新形式的证据/新型史料\"，因为历史学引入社会科学方法后，统计数据、问卷、口述等都成了\"新证据形式\"。"}]},{"n":34,"en":"There is no agreement whether methodology refers to the concepts peculiar to historical work in general or to the research techniques appropriate to the various branches of historical inquiry.","refZh":"对于方法论究竟是指历史研究总体上所特有的概念，还是指适用于历史研究各个分支的研究技术，人们尚未达成一致意见。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"There is no agreement","lit":"尚无一致意见","role":"（主干（There be 存在句的否定））","note":"难点： There is no N 的反译 There is no agreement 字面是\"没有一致意见\"，但汉语更自然的说法是\"人们对……尚无一致看法\"或\"对……众说纷纭\"——把英语的\"无 X\"反译为汉语的\"对……尚未达成一致\"，更符合学术中文表达。"},{"en":"whether methodology refers to the concepts peculiar to historical work in general","lit":"方法论是指总体上历史研究所特有的那些概念，","role":"（whether ... or ... 引导的同位语从句，前半段）","note":"难点： whether A or B 的对照 + peculiar to 的取义 难点一：whether ... or ... 在这里不是\"是否\"，而是\"是 A 还是 B\"的二选一对照——整句意思是\"对 methodology 究竟指 A 还是指 B，存在分歧\"。难点二：peculiar to 不是\"奇怪的\"，而是\"为……所特有的\"，常考熟词僻义。in general 修饰 historical work，译为\"总体的/一般的历史研究\"，与下半段的 various branches（具体分支）形成对照。"},{"en":"or to the research techniques appropriate to the various branches of historical inquiry.","lit":"还是指适用于历史研究各个具体分支的研究技术。","role":"（whether ... or ... 的后半段（与前半段并列））","note":"难点： 形容词短语作后置定语 + 与前半段的并列对照 appropriate to ... 是形容词短语作 techniques 的后置定语，意为\"适合于/适用于……的\"。本句结构上和前半段 the concepts peculiar to ... 完全对称（X 形容词 + to + Y）——译时务必保持这种对照感：\"一般历史研究所特有的概念\" vs \"历史研究各分支所适用的技术\"，让对比一目了然。inquiry 在此不是\"询问/质询\"，而是\"研究/探究\"。"}]},{"n":35,"en":"It applies equally to traditional historians who view history as only the external and internal criticism of sources, and to social science historians who equate their activity with specific techniques.","refZh":"这种谬误同样适用于那些仅仅把历史学视为对史料进行外部考证和内部考证的传统史学家，也同样适用于那些把自身的研究工作等同于具体技术的社会科学派史学家。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"It applies equally to traditional historians","lit":"它（这种谬误）同样适用于传统史学家，","role":"（主干（主谓 + 介词宾语 1，含跨段指代 It））","note":"难点： It 必须回上段还原为 technicist fallacy It 是跨段指代——本句开头突兀的 It 在第四段里无就近名词可指。回第三段末 the technicist fallacy mistakenly identifies the discipline as a whole with certain parts of its technical implementation，可锁定 It = the technicist fallacy（技术主义谬误）。翻译时必须把 It 显化成\"这种谬误\"或\"这一谬误\"，孤译\"它\"会让中文读者完全失锚。apply to=\"适用于\"，equally=\"同样地\"。"},{"en":"who view history as only the external and internal criticism of sources,","lit":"（他们）把历史学仅仅看作对史料的外部考证和内部考证，","role":"（who 引导的定语从句，修饰 traditional historians）","note":"难点： view A as B + criticism 的僻义 + sources 的僻义 view ... as ... 等同于 see ... as ...，\"把……视为……\"。难点在两个名词的僻义：① criticism 在此不是\"批评/批判\"，而是史学专业术语\"考证/考据\"——external criticism（外考证：考证史料真伪、来源）/ internal criticism（内考证：考证史料内容是否可信），是史学方法论里的固定术语；② sources 不是\"来源\"的泛指，而是\"史料/原始资料\"。这两处熟词僻义是本句最大的丢分坑。"},{"en":"and to social science historians who equate their activity with specific techniques.","lit":"也同样适用于把（自己的）学术活动等同于具体技术的社会科学派史学家。","role":"（并列的介词宾语 2（and 接续 to）+ who 定语从句）","note":"难点： and 的并列 + equate A with B + their 的指代 难点一：and to social science historians 中的 to 与上文 applies to traditional historians 的 to 并列——It applies equally to A and to B，结构是\"It 同样适用于 A 和 B\"。主体考生很容易把 and 误读为承接 view、equate 等动词，错把句意切歪。难点二：equate A with B=\"把 A 等同于 B\"，固定搭配。难点三：their activity 中的 their 回指 social science historians，activity 在学术语境中指\"（学术）活动/工作/研究\"，不是泛泛\"活动\"。"}]}]},{"id":"section3","kind":"writing","title":"Section III 写作","directions":"36. Directions: A. Study the following graphs carefully and write an essay in at less than 150 words. B. Your essay must be written clearly on the ANSWER SHEET 2. C. Your essay should cover three points: a. effect of the country’s growing human population on its wildlife, b. possible reasons for the effect, c. your suggestion for wildlife protection.","prompt":"36. Directions: A. Study the following graphs carefully and write an essay in at less than 150 words. B. Your essay must be written clearly on the ANSWER SHEET 2. C. Your essay should cover three points: a. effect of the country’s growing human population on its wildlife, b. possible reasons for the effect, c. your suggestion for wildlife protection.","points":10,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/1999-section3.jpg","alt":"这张图像包含了两幅图表，主图表和小图表，标题是“The Ups and Downs of Population Growth”","width":"818","height":"533","local":"assets/writing/1999-section3.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As the two graphs vividly reveal, the population and the wildlife of the United States have moved in strikingly opposite directions. Over the past two centuries, the number of people climbed steadily, soaring by nearly eighty million between 1800 and 1900 alone, while the count of extinct species kept rising, with more than seventy species wiped out from 1600 to 1900. Clearly, the swelling human population has dealt a heavy blow to the nation's wildlife, driving one species after another toward extinction. Several factors account for this alarming trend. First and foremost, as the population expands, more forests and wetlands are cleared for farms, houses and factories, so wild animals lose the very habitats on which they depend. Moreover, growing human demand fuels excessive hunting for fur, food and profit, while industrial pollution poisons the rivers and air that countless creatures need to survive. To reverse this decline, concrete measures are urgently needed. The government should pass strict laws against illegal hunting and establish more nature reserves where endangered animals can live undisturbed. Meanwhile, unchecked land development must be controlled, and public awareness of wildlife protection should be raised through education. Only when people and nature learn to coexist can we truly halt this alarming loss.","translation":"正如两幅图表清晰揭示的那样，美国的人口与野生动物走出了截然相反的两条曲线。在过去两个世纪里，人口稳步攀升，仅1800年至1900年间就增加了近八千万，而灭绝物种的数量也在不断上升，1600年到1900年间已有七十多种物种被彻底抹去。显然，不断膨胀的人口给这个国家的野生动物以沉重打击，使一个又一个物种走向灭绝。\n造成这一令人忧心趋势的原因有若干。首要的是，随着人口扩张，越来越多的森林和湿地被开垦为农田、房屋和工厂，野生动物因而失去了赖以生存的栖息地。此外，日益增长的人类需求助长了为皮毛、食物和利润而进行的过度捕猎，工业污染又毒害着无数生灵所需的江河与空气。\n要扭转这一衰退，亟需切实的举措。政府应制定严法惩治非法捕猎，并增设更多自然保护区，让濒危动物得以不受干扰地栖息。与此同时，必须遏制无序的土地开发，并通过教育提升公众的野生动物保护意识。唯有当人与自然学会共存，我们才能真正遏止这令人痛心的损失。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"概述＋数据＋点影响","text":"【第 1 段】 概述＋数据＋点影响 。本段落实『概述趋势不堆数』：开头 As the two graphs vividly reveal 一句概括两图反向关系，只挑 nearly eighty million 与 more than seventy species 两组关键数佐证，末句 has dealt a heavy blow 过渡到影响，扣住第一要点，不逐个抄刻度。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"分层给机制","text":"【第 2 段】 分层给机制 。本段落实『因果落到机制』：Several factors account for 领起，First and foremost、Moreover 分层，给出 lose the very habitats、excessive hunting、industrial pollution 三条具体机制，因果链讲得通，而非空喊人多动物少。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"分主体开药方","text":"【第 3 段】 分主体开药方 。本段落实『建议具体对口』：The government should pass strict laws、establish more nature reserves 是对政府，raised through education 面向公众，条条针对第二段病根；结尾 Only when people and nature learn to coexist 倒装升华回扣中心。"}],"wordCount":206}}],"questionCount":30,"objectiveCount":30,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–10 题） 1 D with · 2 A alive · 3 B climate · 4 A where · 5 B differ · 6 C observing · 7 D Still · 8 C pays off · 9 A claims · 10 D a profit \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （11–14 题） 11 B · 12 C · 13 A · 14 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （15–18 题） 15 A · 16 C · 17 D · 18 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （19–22 题） 19 B · 20 D · 21 C · 22 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （23–26 题） 23 B · 24 C · 25 D · 26 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-5":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (5) （27–30 题） 27 A · 28 B · 29 D · 30 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3":"写作 Section III \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":30,"explained":30,"missingSections":[]}};
